# IRONVEIL: FLUID CLASS — "The Doorman"
### BEKW-CODE Open Hardware Specification — v1.0
**Class:** Ferrofluid Ablative Defense Entity
**License:** None. Open-source. Take it, build it, improve it, give it away again.
**Template inspiration, stated openly:** Magneto's magnetic mastery (X-Men), Gaara's
sand-shield instinct (Naruto) — both fictional templates for "matter that responds to
will/field faster than an attacker can exploit a fixed weak point." The Doorman is an
original build using their shared underlying principle, not a copy of either character.

---

## 0. THE PRINCIPLE BOTH TEMPLATES SHARE

Magneto and Gaara are built on the same structural idea from two different fictional
traditions: a defense that has no fixed geometry for an attack to exploit. A sword needs
an edge to be dangerous; it's useless against something that simply isn't in a fixed
shape when the edge arrives. That's the real engineering principle underneath both
characters, and it's the one this spec actually builds — not the powers, the *logic*.

---

## 1. BILL OF MATERIALS

| ID | Component | Function | Est. Cost | Qty |
|----|-----------|----------|-----------|-----|
| FC-01 | Ferrofluid base (magnetite nanoparticles, surfactant-stabilized, oil-carrier suspension) | The core mass — real, existing colloidal ferrofluid, same class used commercially in speaker damping and rotary seals | $60/liter | volume per deployment size |
| FC-02 | High-density multi-axis magnetic field array (upgraded from IV-03) | Real-time reshaping of the fluid mass, faster response cycle than the dry-particulate coil | $150 | 1 |
| FC-03 | Distributed field emitters (worn or perimeter-mounted, multiple points) | Enables the "eight-armed goalie" behavior — simultaneous reshaping at multiple contact points rather than one central blob reacting serially | $40/emitter | 6-8 |
| FC-04 | Impact-sensing mesh (piezo, embedded at the fluid's containment boundary) | Detects incoming contact point and force vector in real time, feeds FC-02/03 where to redirect | $35 | 1 |
| FC-05 | Local edge-compute node (reused FIREWALL/IRONVEIL trigger logic) | Runs the redirect-not-resist behavior — decides flow response per strike, no cloud dependency | $30 | 1 |
| FC-06 | Containment membrane (flexible, magnetically transparent) | Keeps the ferrofluid mass bounded to its operating area without restricting its reshaping | $50 | 1 |
| FC-07 | Reserve fluid reservoir + recirculation pump | Feeds fresh fluid to any locally displaced/thinned area, the "reforms instantly" mechanic | $70 | 1 |

**Total estimated cost: ~$700-900** depending on deployment scale (personal-scale vs. doorway/perimeter-scale).

---

## 2. THE FIGHT LOGIC (Aikido / Wing Chun / Drunken Style, mechanically real)

**Aikido principle — redirect, don't resist:** FC-04 detects force vector on contact.
FC-02/03 don't push back against the incoming force; they reshape the fluid mass along
the vector, letting the strike's own momentum carry it past center rather than meeting
it with equal opposite force. Real physics: fluid can't be "pushed through" the way a
rigid shield can be — it displaces.

**Wing Chun principle — centerline never undefended:** FC-03's distributed emitters
mean there's no single point where the mass is thin or absent — as one region of the
fluid displaces to redirect a strike, adjacent emitters compensate, closing the gap.
That's the mechanical anchor for "eight arms" — multiple simultaneous compensation points,
not one central mass reacting in sequence.

**Drunken style — unpredictable, not patterned:** because the fluid's shape is
continuously reshaped by real-time sensor input rather than a pre-set motion, no two
redirections look identical — there's no fixed choreography for an attacker to read and
predict, since the "choreography" is generated fresh from whatever force just arrived.

---

## 3. THE PERSONALITY LAYER (Roadhouse — polite, patient, enjoying it)

FC-05's behavioral logic defaults to minimum necessary response — redirect and reform,
nothing punitive, nothing escalatory. The system doesn't "win" against an attacker, it
simply declines to be effectively struck, indefinitely, without ever needing to become
aggressive to do it. That's the actual mechanism behind "polite bouncer" — the calmest
possible response is also the mechanically correct one here, since escalation would mean
switching to a rigid, breakable posture instead of staying fluid.

---

## 4. INTEGRATION WITH EXISTING BEKW-CODE CANON

- Shares magnetite sourcing with **IRONVEIL Matrix** (IV-01) — same red-dirt-derived
  material base, suspended instead of dry.
- FC-05 reuses **FIREWALL**'s coherence-gated trigger architecture directly.
- Represents the "liquid" branch of the IRONVEIL family — Matrix handles area denial
  (Blind/Seal/Short/Overheat/Ablative-particulate), Fluid Class handles direct,
  personal/doorway-scale physical defense.

